      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name} \n\n>  I won't discuss the assetbundle security details on a public forum like this, but the cache encryption is client-side.\n\nwut should i have discussed?\n\nObviously the client must always recieve a secret to decrypt the content, but the secret isn't stored like the avatar files. The file is worthless without the key which is why this key is so hard protected. That's basic knowledge.\n\nTLDR, fight against modified clients/cheat clients is a cat and mouse game. It was always, it will always. The fredom of soft- and hardware on PC will always hold doors open for it. To prevent this, we all need to agree and higher security standards, but nobody likes locked ecosystems, where you can't freely install hard-/software.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
